1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,880
Slowly, Franklin brought his knuckle close

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:03,540
to the key.

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,640
A spark jumped across with a tiny snap,

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,340
exactly the kind of spark he had made a

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,300
thousand times in his own room.

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:16,079
Then he touched the key to his Leyden jar

7
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,220
and filled it with electricity from the

8
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:19,780
sky.

9
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,900
It behaved in every way like the

10
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,240
electricity he made with glass and silk.

11
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:28,680
Lightning and the spark in the jar were

12
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,300
the same thing, electricity.

13
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:34,400
And here is the part that most people get

14
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:37,480
wrong. The kite was never struck by

15
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:40,280
lightning. If it had been, Franklin would

16
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:43,680
almost certainly have died. Instead, the

17
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:45,520
kite gathered a little of the storm's

18
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:48,640
electric charge, which ran quietly down

19
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,380
the wet string to the key.

20
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:54,420
It was still dangerous. The next summer, a

21
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:57,100
scientist in Russia called Georg Richmann

22
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,800
was trying a similar experiment with a rod

23
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:02,320
during a storm, and he was killed.

24
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:05,920
Franklin had been careful and lucky.

25
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,960
In October, Franklin published how to do

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,380
the kite experiment in his own newspaper.

27
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:15,320
His letters were read at The Royal Society

28
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,640
in London, and the next year it gave him

29
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:20,280
its highest award, the Copley Medal.

30
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:23,260
But Franklin wasn't only interested in

31
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:27,240
proving an idea. He wanted to use it. If a

32
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:29,840
pointed rod could pull electricity from

33
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:32,660
the sky, could it also keep lightning away

34
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,960
from people's homes?
